#!/usr/bin/env bash
# A live switch draws what a fresh start draws (mobile/devices.md): the
# same screen, shot after a switch inside the running app (theme,
# language, text size) and after a fresh start in that setting, is the
# same pixel for pixel. Lists every region that differs, and fails on any.
#
#   .practices/bin/check-shots [--skip-top PX] FRESH LIVE
#   .practices/bin/check-shots --only-top PX PAGE PLACEHOLDER
#
# FRESH and LIVE are two PNG screenshots, or two folders whose PNGs of
# the same name are compared. --skip-top leaves out the status bar, whose
# clock moves between the shots. The measuring is in shots-diff.mjs.
#
# A placeholder is drawn on the page's own edges (ui/feedback.md): with
# --only-top, only the band above PX is compared, the page loaded against
# its placeholder, the status bar included. Below it they differ anyway.
# Fix the clock first (xcrun simctl status_bar <device> override --time
# 9:41) so the bar matches. On 25 Nov 2026 a placeholder stopped at the
# status bar while its page ran under it, and cut the page's glow off.
#
# Why: in Obálka a "Testovací" pill read "Testovac" after a switch to the
# dark theme and was whole after a restart (2026-11-16). Its box kept its
# size; only the last glyph was gone, and every check looked at fresh
# starts.
#
# Needs Node 18+; without it it fails, never passes.

# shellcheck source=lib.sh
. "$(dirname "$0")/lib.sh"

if ! command -v node >/dev/null; then
    echo "check-shots: needs Node 18 or newer, and there is no node on PATH." >&2
    exit 2
fi
exec node "$(dirname "$0")/shots-diff.mjs" "$@"
